🔁 Overview
| Feature       | `Collections.synchronizedMap`                 | `ConcurrentHashMap`                                    |
| ------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| Thread Safety | ✅ Yes (synchronized)                          | ✅ Yes (internally concurrent)                          |
| Performance   | ❌ Slower (locks entire map)                   | ✅ Faster (locks only portions)                         |
| Locking       | Locks the **entire map**                      | Uses **segment-level locking** or fine-grained locking |
| Iteration     | Must **manually synchronize**                 | Safe iteration **without extra sync**                  |
| Null Support  | ✅ Allows **one null key** and **null values** | ❌ **Does not allow** null keys or null values          |
| Introduced In | Java 1.2 (`Collections`)                      | Java 5 (`java.util.concurrent`)                        |
| Best For      | Simple, low-concurrency apps                  | High-concurrency, performance-critical apps            |


🔧 1. Collections.synchronizedMap Example
java
Copy
Edit
Map<String, String> map = Collections.synchronizedMap(new HashMap<>());

synchronized (map) { // manual sync required for iteration
    for (String key : map.keySet()) {
        System.out.println(key + " = " + map.get(key));
    }
}
🚀 2. ConcurrentHashMap Example
java
Copy
Edit
Map<String, String> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

// No manual sync needed
for (String key : map.keySet()) {
    System.out.println(key + " = " + map.get(key));
}
🔍 Internal Working
| Feature     | `synchronizedMap`          | `ConcurrentHashMap`                   |
| ----------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Locking     | One lock for entire map    | Locks **only buckets (segments)**     |
| Scalability | Poor under high threads    | Excellent under high threads          |
| Blocking    | All threads block on write | Threads block only on affected bucket |


⚠️ Null Handling
| Map Type            | Null Key | Null Value |
| ------------------- | -------- | ---------- |
| `HashMap`           | ✅ Yes    | ✅ Yes      |
| `synchronizedMap`   | ✅ Yes    | ✅ Yes      |
| `ConcurrentHashMap` | ❌ No     | ❌ No       |


Trying to insert null into ConcurrentHashMap will throw NullPointerException.

✅ Summary: When to Use What?
| Scenario                                            | Use This                       |
| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Simple app, low concurrency                         | `Collections.synchronizedMap`  |
| High-concurrency app (e.g. web server, thread pool) | `ConcurrentHashMap`            |
| You need null keys/values                           | `HashMap` or `synchronizedMap` |
| You need high throughput under heavy load           | `ConcurrentHashMap`            |


